WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:58.970
[GHIN] I don't care how much of a bad ass
he used to be; now he's just a cook.

38
00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.190
I wouldn't have to break a
sweat to kill this old fart.

39
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.900
I'll spare him, but you have to leave.

40
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.860
Please, don't make this any
harder, Sanji. Just leave.

41
00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.740
Don't force me to kill both of you.

42
00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.290
Run away... Not a chance!

43
00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.410
[gasps]

44
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.330
[SANJI] You look even dumber
at gunpoint, Old Man.

45
00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.880
What kind of example do you think
you're setting for all the other cooks?

46
00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.710
Hah! I don't need a lecture
from a brat like you.

47
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.470
Would you stop calling me names?!

48
00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.430
Quit treating me like a kid!

49
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:37.890
This is crazy!

50
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.600
Sanji wouldn't abandon
Zeff now would he?

51
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.310
[SANJI] Ghin, point that gun at me.

52
00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.730
[ZEFF grunts]

53
00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.730
Hey, but what if you die?!

54
00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.020
Shut up.

55
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.980
Sanji, why you?

56
00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.070
[PEARL] Someone's eager to die.

57
00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.280
Lucky for you, I'd be
more than happy to oblige.

58
00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.990
Allow me...

59
00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.160
It would be my pleasure to beat
you to a bloody, lifeless pulp.

60
00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.580
[grunts]

61
00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.080
[PEARL] The absolutely natural Pearl...

62
00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:06.920
[SANJI gasps]

63
00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.580
[PEARL] Surprise!

64
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.130
[SANJI grunts]

65
00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.550
Sanji!

66
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.010
Why didn't you dodge that?!

67
00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.760
[SANJI grunts]
Because if I did,

68
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.300
that rat over there would
pull the trigger on Zeff.

69
00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.100
[huffs]

70
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.260
[GHIN] Why are you doing this?

71
00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.680
Just leave the restaurant
peacefully and no one gets hurt.

72
00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.640
Please!

73
00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.100
This restaurant is that old man's life!

74
00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.780
[SANJI] I've already taken everything
else that man holds dear.

75
00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:43.370
[SANJI] His power... his dreams...

76
00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:46.540
[SANJI grunts]
So, while I'm around...

77
00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.290
... I'm not gonna let anything
else get taken from him!

78
00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.340
[ZEFF grunts]

79
00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.460
Behind you!

80
00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.550
[PEARL] Pearl... Cymbals!

81
00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:57.130
[CARNE] Sanji!

82
00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.760
[LUFFY grunting]

83
00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.010
[SANJI groans]

84
00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.850
The All Blue?

85
00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.810
[SANJI] Yeah! It's out there somewhere.

86
00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:09.100
And I'll bet it's even
awesomer than they say it is!

87
00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:15.740
<b>Because of a Dream</b>

88
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.740
[COOK A] Stop being a doofus.

89
00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:21.660
<b>The Orbit
A Passenger Ship</b>

90
00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.530
That's just a fairy tale
for seafaring cooks.

91
00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:21.950
[COOK B] Don't get me wrong,

92
00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.910
we've all had our little
fantasies about it,

93
00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.620
but you gotta remember
that it's just a dream.

94
00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:31.080
A dream? Well I'm gonna find the All
Blue, then we'll see who's dreaming.

95
00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:31.080
<b>Sanji (9 Years Ago)
Passenger Ship
Cook's Apprentice</b>

96
00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.460
That's quite the quest. Good luck!

97
00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:34.800
All right there little man.

98
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.800
Tell me, do you even know what
kind of place the All Blue is?

99
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.050
[SANJI] Yeah, I do. I'm not an idiot.

100
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.970
The All Blue is a place where
fish from all four seas live.

101
00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:49.940
There're fish from East Blue, the West Blue,
the North Blue, and the South Blue.

102
00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.150
To cooks who have taken to the sea,
it's an irresistible paradise!

103
00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.190
I'll find it!

104
00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.780
Oh yeah! That place is a goldmine!

105
00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.240
It's got fish and plants
from all over the world!

106
00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.830
Any chef would jump at
the chance to cook there!

107
00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:08.330
True. The cooks I know would
risk life and limb to find it.

108
00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.670
[COOK A] Yeah! Well, if it were real.

109
00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.330
Oh?

110
00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.290
You think a miracle sea like the
All Blue could actually exist?

111
00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.960
Think about it kid, it's impossible.

112
00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:21.800
[COOK C] Ha, ha! I bet it's probably
just a lie told by some daydreaming cook.

113
00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.800
[COOK A] Okay, enough
with the silly stories.

114
00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.310
Get out there and collect
some plates, Sanji.

115
00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.270
[SANJI] Hmph.

116
00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.480
[COOK A] Aw man. What a waste!

117
00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.810
They left behind plates and plates
full of this delicious grub.

118
00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.110
[COOK C] This one's barely been touched!

119
00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.980
It's pretty good stuff too. I
thought they'd love it for sure.

120
00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.360
[COOK B] If you ask me,
the customers these days are spoiled.

121
00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.070
It's way gross to eat
the leftovers of strangers.

122
00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.280
You should just let me
throw that stuff away.

123
00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:50.200
That kind of talk proves you gotta whole lot
to learn, so listen up, shorty.

124
00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.670
If you choose life on the high
seas, you gotta be resourceful.

125
00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:56.090
The ocean is a strange
and unpredictable place,

126
00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.800
where wasting food
could be a fatal mistake.

127
00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.380
So, why don't you have some? Heh?

128
00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.510
No way!

129
00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:03.220
[COOK II giggles]

130
00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.050
[passengers screaming]

131
00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:08.180
Calm down, people!
Panicking won't help!

132
00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.890
[SANJI, COOKS] Hm?

133
00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:10.890
[SAILOR B grunts]

134
00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.230
Pirates are here!

135
00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.110
[COOKS whimper]

136
00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:16.810
[gasps]
What?

137
00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.690
Pirates?

138
00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.900
[SAILOR C] That ship.

139
00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.030
It's Red Foot Zeff
and the Cook Pirates!

140
00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.160
[SANJI grunts]

141
00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:30.290
[SAILOR B] They're back...
from the Grand Line!

142
00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.210
[PIRATES chuckle]

143
00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.920
<b>"Red Leg" Zeff
Cook Pirates</b>

144
00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.500
[ZEFF laughs]

145
00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.340
I take it you're the
infamous pirate captain

146
00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.720
Red Foot Zeff.

147
00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.600
So, what do you want?

148
00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.600
Steal!

149
00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.430
[PIRATES yelling]

150
00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.140
[ZEFF] Steal everything
that isn't nailed down!

151
00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:58.560
[passengers screaming]

152
00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.400
[SANJI] Those bastards!

153
00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.070
I refuse to die at the
hands of those animals!

154
00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:06.450
[PIRATE 2] Whoa, look at this!

155
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.950
Hey, Killer, if you're not careful,
you might just put someone's eye out with that.

156
00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:15.000
He got me. Look, I'm bleeding.

157
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.750
Shut up! You mongrels
better stay away from me!

158
00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:20.880
[COOK A yelps] Sanji!

159
00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.590
Stop it! You'll make them mad!

160
00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:28.180
[ZEFF] A bit young to have a death wish,
but that's no reason not to grant it.

161
00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.510
All right, you jerks!

162
00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:33.020
If I'm dying here, then I'm
takin' some of you with me!

163
00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:33.720
[SANJI gasps]

164
00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:34.980
[SANJI] Ah!

165
00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.440
Sanji!

166
00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.150
Wow, good one!

167
00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.690
Yeah, that was brutal!

168
00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.860
[PIRATES chuckle]

169
00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.160
[SANJI grunts]

170
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.790
[SANJI] I'm not gonna die.

171
00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:58.080
Not here... Ah!

172
00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:03.050
I've got to live... so that
I can find the All Blue!

173
00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:06.510
[ALL laughing]

174
00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.840
[PIRATE 3] He said, "the All Blue!"

175
00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:11.850
[PIRATE 4] Pretty ambitious!

176
00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:13.350
[PIRATE 1] Oh, that's a good one!

177
00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:17.480
Hey Captain, should we tell the
little tyke it doesn't exist?

178
00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.440
[COOKS whimpering]

179
00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:21.060
He won't shut up!

180
00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:19.730
That fool...

181
00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.310
[ZEFF growls]

182
00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:32.240
I'm not gonna draw my last breath
until I've seen the All Blue.

183
00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.120
[PIRATE 3] Captain!

184
00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.490
I recommend we withdraw, immediately!

185
00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:38.460
This storm is way bigger than expected!

186
00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.920
[ZEFF] All right men, playtime's over.

187
00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.960
Let's load up the treasure
and get out of here.

188
00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.180
[whimpering]

189
00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:51.970
[ALL yelling]

190
00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:52.970
[gasps]

191
00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.020
[SANJI grunts]

192
00:08:58.270 --> 00:08:59.480
Sanji!

193
00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:00.310
[ZEFF grumbles]

194
00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.190
[PIRATE 2] The captain!

195
00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.320
Damn brat!

196
00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:15.530
[PIRATE 5] Captain!

197
00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.620
[PIRATE 3] Why'd he risk
his life for one measly kid?

198
00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.420
[ZEFF] The brat finally wakes up.

199
00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.290
You're lucky to be alive, you know.

200
00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.090
[SANJI groans] You!

201
00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:10.010
[ZEFF] Moving isn't a good idea.

202
00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.680
You're still pretty banged up
from the beating you took.

203
00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:13.590
[SANJI gasps]

204
00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.890
[SANJI] What about the ships?

205
00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:16.180
[ZEFF] Who knows?

206
00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.600
It was terrible storm.

207
00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.520
Our ships were most likely destroyed.

208
00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.600
Seems we're the only survivors.

209
00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:28.320
Washed ashore on a desolate rock, without
so much as a coconut tree to give us food.

210
00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.730
Sure, there are fish in the sea,

211
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.700
but the rock has been curved
by the waves in such a manner

212
00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:37.410
that we wouldn't be able to climb
back up, if we ever went down.

213
00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:38.580
Sad, isn't it?

214
00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:40.830
This is all your fault, Old Man!

215
00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.290
I hope you die!

216
00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.920
[ZEFF] You can whine all
you want, it won't help.

217
00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:49.380
If nobody comes, we'll just dry up
and become two more skeletons in the sea.

218
00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.260
Skeletons?

219
00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:52.550
Really?

220
00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:55.840
[ZEFF] That bag there...
It's your share of it.

221
00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.590
Ah!

222
00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.720
[ZEFF] It's some of the food
that washed up.

223
00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.930
Should be about five days worth.

224
00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:05.690
It's not much, but it's
better than nothin'.

225
00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:10.440
If you ration it out, it'll last longer,
so use your head when you eat.

226
00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.280
Good thing we're both cooks, huh?

227
00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.400
Hey, wait!

228
00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.450
Is that bag your share of the food?!

229
00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:17.950
You got way more than me!

230
00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.450
You fat, old pig!

231
00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.040
[ZEFF] Of course I get more food...

232
00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:27.750
I'm a grown man, so I need more
to survive than a runt like you.

233
00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:32.000
You should be grateful that
I'm sharing any of it with you.

234
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.970
Don't expect any pity
from me, you little brat!

235
00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.970
[growling]

236
00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:39.470
Bastard!

237
00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.940
[ZEFF] Get to the other side of
this rock and watch for ships.

238
00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:48.100
Let me know as soon as you see one.

239
00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.860
Until then, don't bother talkin'
to me or movin' from your post.

240
00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:55.280
That'll just waste energy,
and we can't afford that.

241
00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:57.030
Good luck.

242
00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:58.280
Screw you, gramps.

243
00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:01.160
I'm not saying anything
if I see a ship.

244
00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:04.700
I'll be fine. I have five
whole days worth of food.

245
00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.460
We'll definitely see a ship
or two before I run out.

246
00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:08.620
I'm sure of it.

247
00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.130
Just to be extra safe, I'll
divide it up for twenty days.

248
00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:14.380
That's more than enough
time to get rescued.

249
00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:18.180
I guess all I gotta
do now is sit and wait.

250
00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:21.050
Easy! I'll make it
through this thing...

251
00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.970
No problem!

252
00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.900
[SANJI grunts]

253
00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.780
Didn't see a ship today.

254
00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:42.070
That's all right.
It'll only be a few more days.

255
00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.420
[SANJI] I don't wanna die...

256
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.220
[SANJI weakly]
This is it...

257
00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.390
One moldy piece of bread.

258
00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.730
[COOK A] Aw man, what a waste.

259
00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.900
They left behind plates and plates
full of this delicious grub.

260
00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:22.070
[SANJI] It's way gross to eat
the leftovers of strangers.

261
00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:25.200
You should just let me
throw that stuff away.

262
00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:28.500
So, why don't you have some... huh?

263
00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:31.870
[SANJI] No way!

264
00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:39.590
– [sniffling]
– [stomach growls]

265
00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.970
[SANJI yelps]

266
00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.100
[SANJI screams]

267
00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:51.770
[SANJI gasps]

268
00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.480
[SANJI] of bread.

269
00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:33.770
[SANJI] I wonder...

270
00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.060
Is the geezer dead yet?

271
00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:46.070
[SANJI grunting]

272
00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.740
And he's still got food!

273
00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.370
A lot of food!

274
00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.000
[SANJI gasps]
He's alive...

275
00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.160
So much.

276
00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.330
There's so much left!

277
00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:02.840
I've got to get that food.

278
00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.970
It's not fair that he has
so much more than me.

279
00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.800
Besides, this is all his fault!

280
00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.650
[ZEFF] What're you doing here, ya' brat?

281
00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:21.610
[gasps]

282
00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:23.940
[ZEFF] Are you here
because ya' saw a ship?

283
00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:27.820
[panting]

284
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.700
I came over here to
steal your food, Old Man.

285
00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.950
If you wanna kill me for it, go ahead.

286
00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:36.540
Soon enough I'll starve, so
it makes no difference to me.

287
00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.920
[SANJI panting]

288
00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:01.440
[ZEFF] Didn't I tell you not to come
over here unless you saw a ship?

289
00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.940
[SANJI] Why?

290
00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.240
You said it's... food.

291
00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.870
[ZEFF] Strange, isn't it?

292
00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.530
We have all this money and
yet, we're going to starve.

293
00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.370
It's only treasure...

294
00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:18.540
It's worthless.

295
00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.090
[labored breathing]

296
00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:27.550
[SANJI] Hey! What's
going on here, Old Man?

297
00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:29.010
Where's your food?

298
00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.800
You had to have eaten something!

299
00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.930
Now, where is it?

300
00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:33.100
I'm talking to you!

301
00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:34.720
Answer me!

302
00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:35.810
[SANJI gasps]

303
00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:39.940
[SANJI gasps]

304
00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.950
What happened to your leg?

305
00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.070
The food...

306
00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.820
Did you give me all
of the food you had?

307
00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.790
I did.

308
00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:58.660
And you had to have known
that without that leg,

309
00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.710
you'd never be a pirate again.

310
00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:02.080
[ZEFF] That's right.

311
00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.460
[gasps] You old fool.

312
00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.090
Why'd you help me?

313
00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:11.300
It doesn't make sense to
sacrifice so much for me!

314
00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:13.140
So, why?

315
00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:14.350
Tell me!

316
00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:16.680
[ZEFF] Because...

317
00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:20.770
For my entire life I've
had the same dream as you.

318
00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:25.980
The All Blue...

319
00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:29.190
But... your men said
that it doesn't exist.

320
00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.110
[ZEFF] Of course it does!

321
00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.780
Never mind them.

322
00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.620
When the time comes,
head to the Grand Line.

323
00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:37.700
That's where the All
Blue is sure to be.

324
00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:44.880
My days as a pirate are done,
but you have your whole life to find it.

325
00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:46.420
[ZEFF sighs]

326
00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:48.670
Don't die, now! Get up!

327
00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.800
C'mon, Old Man!

328
00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:54.510
Don't you dare give up!

329
00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:56.850
[ZEFF] I wonder...

330
00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:00.640
How many men have lost their
lives cursing the ocean,

331
00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:05.190
knowing that it will
soon be their grave.

332
00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:09.230
This isn't the first time I've been
hungry enough to look death in the eyes,

333
00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:12.280
and my thoughts are the same each time.

334
00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:17.280
It is always my deepest wish that there
be a restaurant in the middle of the sea.

335
00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:18.700
[SANJI] A restaurant?

336
00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:22.250
[ZEFF] Yeah, I was thinking that if
I make it out of this mess alive,

337
00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:26.210
I'd like to build a restaurant
as my final purpose in life.

338
00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:28.710
Great! And I'll even help you do it!

339
00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.800
So, don't die, okay? Ha!

340
00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:31.510
Ha, ha!

341
00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:32.880
A weak little brat like you

342
00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:35.140
couldn't be much good for anything.

343
00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:37.100
Then, I'll become strong!

344
00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:40.890
[whimpers]
So... Don't die!

345
00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.890
[whimpering]

346
00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.490
Help!

347
00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.620
The geezer needs help!

348
00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:58.330
Over here!

349
00:18:58.330 --> 00:18:59.790
Please help!

350
00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:00.740
Please, please!

351
00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.700
Help us!

352
00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.460
[ZEFF groans]

353
00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:06.330
[SANJI] Hey!

354
00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.380
Hey!

355
00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:12.340
Over here! Help us!
This way! Please, please!

356
00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.760
Over here! Over here!

357
00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:17.340
Help, help! This way!

358
00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:17.890
Please!

359
00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:22.930
[SANJI] That old coot...

360
00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:26.850
He gave up his leg
so that I could live!

361
00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.730
[ALL gasping]

362
00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:32.820
[SANJI grunts]

363
00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.820
There's no way to repay the
old geezer for his kindness,

364
00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:37.910
unless I risk my life for him!

365
00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:46.670
Why? Why are you standing, Sanji?

366
00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:49.580
Stay down!

367
00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.250
'Fraid I can't do that.

368
00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.760
It's a little too much like giving up.

369
00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.220
[COOKS gasp]

370
00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:57.590
Idiot! They'll kill you!

371
00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:01.050
[LUFFY grunting]

372
00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:03.390
You little brat!

373
00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:06.520
Ha! That is so very refined of you!

374
00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:11.480
But, this restaurant will be closing soon,
and it'll open again for business...

375
00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.980
... as a pirate ship.

376
00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.070
[LUFFY grunts]

377
00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:15.990
[LUFFY yells]

378
00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.030
No! Don't!

379
00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:18.910
Ghin'll shoot the old man!

380
00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:20.120
